  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Integrated Border Management in Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action will sustain the development of capacities, instruments and infrastructure necessary to effectively implement integrated border management in Pakistan. Priorities include support to Pakistan&#xbf;s nascent strategic border governance framework, system integration, strengthened operational performance of agencies at borders to detect and intercept irregular migration attempts, improvements to the investigative process targeting facilitators, tools and modus operandi of migrant smugglers and traffickers, and overall improvements to the professionalisation of border agencies in the areas of anti-corruption, gender mainstreaming, human rights and human resources management. The action will also keep developing regional and international coordination and cooperation between Pakistan&#xbf;s border agencies and partners in countries along migration routes and facilitate information sharing with the EU. This aims to strengthen combined responses to active and emerging irregular migration trends with regional and international partners, as well as support the exposure and integration of international good practices into Pakistan&#xbf;s national response.</narrative>
  </description>
